{
  "esm": "1.3.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "DimensionlessLiteralWarning",
    "description": "Pins the esm-spec §4.8.6 warning units_dimensionless_literal_mismatch. Equations 0-6 are one per pattern class of the bare-literal impact study and each WARNS: under the current rule a bare literal is neutral and the check is skipped or passes, while read as dimensionless at scale 1 it is a dimension or scale mismatch. Equations 7-14 are controls that must NOT warn: the literal zero stays neutral (max, ifelse branch, ic, comparison), a unit-bearing const carries its unit, and a dimensionless literal in a dimensionless context agrees. Reaction 0's rate warns (exp(-1370 / T)); reaction 1's does not. The document is VALID: at this stage the warning never changes validity.",
    "authors": [
      "Chris Tessum with Claude"
    ],
    "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z"
  },
  "models": {
    "Literals": {
      "variables": {
